'''Hyperdrive pods''',<ref name="CE">''[[Star Wars Character Encyclopedia: Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> also known as '''hyperspace pods''',<ref name="Imperial probe droid">{{SWE|technology|probot|Imperial probe droid}}</ref> '''probot pods''',<ref name="Warhead Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/star-wars-rebels/warhead-episode-guide|text="Warhead" Episode Guide &#124; Star Wars Rebels}}</ref> or '''pod ships''',<ref name="Starfighters">''[[Star Wars Encyclopedia of Starfighters and Other Vehicles]]''</ref> were single-use [[hyperspace]]-capable pods that delivered [[probe droid]]s to their destinations. Consisting of little more than a powerful [[hyperdrive]] and a [[sublight engine]] housed in a protective shield packed with [[sensor]]s, such pods were designed to come down rapidly, mimicking a crashing [[meteorite]] in order to avoid detection. Cushioned snugly inside the pod with its [[Manipulator arm|arms]] retracted, the probe droid used an umbilical to monitor the status and location of its transport. To prevent damage to the droid, said umbilical was withdrawn right before landing.<ref name="Build R2 15">[[Star Wars: Build Your Own R2-D2 9|''Star Wars: Build Your Own R2-D2'' 9]]</ref> [[X3-13]]s were specialized hyperdrive pods used to deploy [[E-XD-series infiltrator droid]]s.<ref name="Warhead Episode Guide" />

